      "category": "steering",
      "title": "Electric Power Steering Failure — 'Direção Elétrica Avariada' Warning and Sudden Loss of Assist",
      "description": "Brazilian Ka III owners report a recurring electric power steering (EPS) fault in which assist suddenly cuts out while driving: the steering becomes very heavy, multiple instrument cluster warning lights illuminate, and the message 'Direção elétrica avariada' (electric steering damaged) is displayed. The fault is often intermittent — assist returns after switching the car off and on — and dealers frequently fail to reproduce it or misdiagnose it as a weak battery. Complaint-site records on Reclame Aqui include cases diagnosed as manufacturing defects in the steering rack/column and owners experiencing the failure repeatedly after repairs, including in vehicles still under warranty.",
      "solution": "Have the EPS system scanned for fault codes and the battery/charging system verified first, since low system voltage can trigger assist cutout. Persistent cases typically require replacement of the electric steering column motor/ECU or the complete steering rack assembly. Document occurrences and pursue warranty or consumer-protection channels for newer vehicles, as the failure mode (loss of assist while moving) is safety-relevant.",
      "severity": "high",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "symptoms": [
        "Steering suddenly becomes very heavy while driving",
        "'Direção elétrica avariada' (electric steering damaged) message on the dash",
        "Multiple warning lights illuminate at the same time",
        "Fault is intermittent — steering works normally after restarting the car",
        "Problem recurs even after dealer repairs or battery replacement"
      ],
