      "title": "Recall: Cracked Driver Airbag Module Mounting Hook in Steering Wheel (2019 Ka Hatch/Sedan)",
      "description": "In March 2019, Ford Brazil recalled Ka Hatch and Sedan model-year 2019 vehicles manufactured between February 11 and 19, 2019 (chassis range K8293090 to K8327710). During production of the steering wheel frame, a crack may have formed in one of the mounting hooks that secure the driver's airbag module. In a frontal collision that triggers airbag deployment, the damaged module could detach from the steering wheel, compromising airbag function and increasing the risk of injury to occupants. The recall was registered with Procon-SP and publicized by the São Paulo state government.",
      "solution": "Take the vehicle to a Ford dealership for free inspection and, if necessary, steering wheel replacement. Owners can confirm whether their chassis is affected via Ford Brazil's recall lookup (ford.com.br), the FordPass app, or Ford customer service at 0800 703 3673.",
